statement:
Let $ABC$ be an acute triangle and let $K$ be a point on the extension of $BC$ beyond $C$. The line through $K$ parallel to $AB$ contains a point $P\ne K$ with $BP=BK$, and the line through $K$ parallel to $AC$ contains a point $Q\ne K$ with $CQ=CK$. The circumcircle of triangle $KPQ$ meets line $AK$ again at $T$. Prove that
1. $\angle BTC+\angle APB=\angle CQA$;
2. $AP\cdot BT\cdot CQ=AQ\cdot CT\cdot BP$.
